#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:282
msgid "I do not see the banner on my website."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:282
msgid "You probably made a choice already: use Preview banner on the Dashboard, or open the website in a private window. Check that the banner is switched on. After an update or a settings change, clear your page cache and CDN once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:283
msgid "Consent Records stay empty."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:283
msgid "Records must be switched on (Settings → Consent records). Click \"Test record saving\" in Consent Records: it shows whether a firewall or security plugin blocks the records. Old cached pages still carry the old script, so clear the page cache."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:284
msgid "\"The scan could not finish\" with a reason."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:284
msgid "\"Your login or this page has expired\": reload the page. \"A security plugin, firewall or the host blocked the request\": allow admin-ajax.php for logged-in administrators. \"The server had an error or ran out of time\": try again; if it repeats, check the PHP error log. Short hiccups are retried automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:285
msgid "The scan report shows \"Not loaded by your website\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:285
msgid "These services were seen in your browser during \"Scan now\", but no page of your website and not your Google Tag Manager loads them: they come from a browser extension or another tool, so they are not listed. If your website does use one of them (for example loaded by a plugin's own script), add it under Cookies → Add a cookie yourself → add all cookies of a known service."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:286
msgid "The daily email reports a \"new third-party file\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:286
msgid "A script, frame or stylesheet from another website that the plugin does not know. Look at its full address in Cookies → Scan report (details) → Other third-party files. If it tracks visitors, add it under Settings → Your own blocking rules; otherwise there is nothing to do."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:287
msgid "A video or map shows a placeholder instead of the content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:287
msgid "That is intended: YouTube, Google Maps and similar services set cookies, so they wait until the visitor allows their category (Google Maps and YouTube: Marketing). The placeholder has a button to load the content once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:288
msgid "How do I test the privacy signal (GPC)?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:288
msgid "Firefox: Settings → Privacy → \"Tell websites not to sell or share my data\"; Brave sends it by default. Open your website: no banner, the chosen categories stay off, and Consent Records shows a GPC record."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:289
msgid "The Dashboard warns about another consent plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:289
msgid "Two banners would block each other. Deactivate the other plugin once this banner is set up."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:290
msgid "Does the plugin make my website compliant?"
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/views/tab-help.php:290
msgid "It gives you the tools: consent before optional cookies, fair choices, proof of consent and a cookie list. Your setup and your privacy policy also matter, so let a privacy professional check them."
msgstr ""

